WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.090
Welcome back to the second drink of The Merger.
欢迎回到《合并》这一集的第二杯酒。

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.850
Director Ken Whittingham joins us for this episode.
导演肯·惠廷汉姆参加了我们这一期的节目。

3
00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.370
And one of my favorite things he shares with us
他分享的内容中，我最喜欢的一点是

4
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.230
is how strategic they were
他们对于新员工的座位安排

5
00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.250
with where all of the new employees would sit
在邓德·米夫林办公区里

6
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.770
in the Dunder Mifflin bullpen.
是多么有策略性。

7
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.050
You know, and that really helped shape
你知道，这确实有助于塑造

8
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.750
some of these new storylines
一些新的故事情节，

9
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.010
with the Stanford branch joining the Scranton branch.
随着斯坦福分公司并入斯克兰顿分公司。

10
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:23.170
I love that as well.
我也很喜欢这一点。

11
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.150
I thought that was one of, like,
我觉得这是，怎么说呢，

12
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.290
when I think about our whole series rewatch
当我回顾我们整个系列的重温，

13
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.090
and different interviews we did with people,
以及我们对不同人员进行的采访时，

14
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.630
I felt like that was one of, like,
我觉得这是，怎么说呢，

15
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.290
A key nugget.
一个关键的干货。

16
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:33.770
Yeah.
没错。

17
00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:41.710
You know, we also talk about who can see each other from their desks and which characters are no longer in each other's line of sight.
你知道，我们还谈到了谁能从办公桌看到谁，以及哪些角色不再处于彼此的视线范围内。

18
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.270
Yeah.
是啊。

19
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.170
Loved that.
我很喜欢那个。

20
00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:44.030
Loved that.
我很喜欢那个。

21
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:50.390
Jenna, you shared how you realized that Pam will no longer look up and see Jim at his desk anymore.
珍娜，你分享了你是如何意识到帕姆再也不能抬头看到吉姆坐在办公桌前了。

22
00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.670
Yeah, his back is to her.
是的，他背对着她。

23
00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:52.310
That's right.
没错。

24
00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:59.030
And there was a deleted scene between Jim and Pam where they're all flirty flirt and it's annoying the crap out of Ryan.
吉姆和帕姆之间有一个删减片段，他们在那儿打情骂俏，把瑞安烦得要死。

25
00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.530
because Pam has basically walked up to chat to Jim
因为帕姆基本上是走过来找吉姆聊天，

26
00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.530
because his back is to her.
因为他背对着她。

27
00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.710
So she can't like make eye contact with him.
所以她没法和他进行眼神交流。

28
00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.070
We talked a little bit about this moment,
我们之前稍微聊过这个时刻，

29
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.090
but we didn't play it.
但我们没有播放它。

30
00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.470
And I think we should hear it.
我觉得我们应该听听看。

31
00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.680
This is weird with you facing the other way.
你背对着我，感觉真奇怪。

32
00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.580
Yeah, I never even knew that part of the office existed.
是啊，我以前都不知道办公室还有那一块区域。

33
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.900
Hey, who's that guy?
嘿，那个人是谁？

34
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.440
That's Stanley Hudson.
那是斯坦利·哈德森。

35
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.020
Huh.
哦。

36
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.520
He's one of our salesmen.
他是我们的销售员之一。

37
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.600
Seems like a nice enough guy.
看起来是个不错的人。

38
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.440
Oh, very.
哦，非常不错。

39
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.440
What about, uh...
那关于，呃……

40
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.320
That is...
那是……

41
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:38.680
Janet Fenstermaker.
珍妮特·芬斯特梅克。

42
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:39.140
Really?
真的吗？

43
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.700
You should say hi.
你应该去打个招呼。

44
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.360
Use her full name.
叫她的全名。

45
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.340
Thank you for all of this.
谢谢你所做的一切。

46
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.200
This is so helpful.
这太有帮助了。

47
00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:46.460
You know what?
你知道吗？

48
00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:47.680
One last question.
最后一个问题。

49
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.220
Who is that fine, older gentleman in the corner?
角落里那位风度翩翩的老绅士是谁？

50
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.800
That is Creed Bratton.
那是克里德·布拉顿。

51
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.100
He has four toes, and he fought in the Civil War.
他有四个脚趾，而且他参加过南北战争。

52
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.040
For the North?
为北方军？

53
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.160
For both sides.
为双方都打过。

54
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.440
Whoever paid more.
谁给的钱多就为谁打。

55
00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:02.960
Obviously.
显而易见。

56
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:03.480
Yeah.
是啊。

57
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:04.840
Hey, sorry.
嘿，抱歉。

58
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.620
Seriously, can you guys—I'm trying to get some work done.
说真的，你们能不能——我正试着做点工作呢。

59
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:08.920
Sorry, man.
抱歉，伙计。

60
00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.980
I love Ryan so much.
我太爱瑞安了。

61
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:11.500
So much.
非常爱。

62
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.980
And you know who she's talking about when she says the Janet—
而且你知道她说珍妮特的时候指的是谁——

63
00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.780
Is that Phyllis?
那是菲利斯吗？

64
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.460
Meredith.
是梅雷迪思。

65
00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.260
Oh, okay.
哦，好的。

66
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:26.440
Well, also this episode, we talk about Andy's nifty gifty bags, and we talked about the fakie bag.
另外，这一集我们聊到了安迪的精美礼品袋，还聊到了那个假礼品袋。

67
00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.660
that that was a prop bag that, you know,
那个其实是道具袋，你知道的，

68
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.020
we would use when we were filming
我们拍摄时会用到它，

69
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.120
because they were silent.
因为它没有声音。

70
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.600
And we sort of mentioned we weren't sure
我们当时提到不太确定

71
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.040
like what those bags were,
那些袋子到底是什么材质，

72
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.800
but Angela, you said someone wrote in and told us.
但安吉拉，你说有人写信告诉我们了。

73
00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:42.140
Yes, thank you, Emma B, for writing in to tell us
是的，谢谢艾玛·B写信告诉我们

74
00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.580
that those type of bags are actually made of vinyl.
那种袋子其实是乙烯基做的。

75
00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:46.380
Oh.
哦。

76
00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.800
Yeah, so they hardly make any noise
对，所以它们几乎不会发出声音，

77
00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.240
and that helps the sound department.
这对录音部门很有帮助。

78
00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:51.840
And Jenna, you'll love this.
而且珍娜，你一定会喜欢这个。

79
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.680
She called it a quote, Foley fun fact.
她称之为“拟音趣闻”。

80
00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:56.560
Oh, I love that.
哦，我喜欢这个。

81
00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.400
Foley fun fact.
拟音趣闻。

82
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.100
After Jack Foley.
以杰克·福利命名。

83
00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:00.620
Right.
没错。

84
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:09.340
Yes, you know I love movie making trivia and Jack Foley is the person who developed all of the sound effect techniques that were used in the early days of filmmaking.
是的，你知道我喜欢电影制作的冷知识，杰克·福利就是开发了电影早期所有音效技术的人。

85
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.900
You've seen it sometime in movies where they're watching it live and they're making these noises using different things.
你有时在电影里看到他们现场观看并利用各种东西制造出那些声音。

86
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:22.100
Well, if you do the Universal Studios tour, at least here in California, they have a whole like show.
如果你去环球影城参观，至少在加州这边，他们有一个完整的表演。

87
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.680
It's like the Foley artist show.
就像是拟音师表演。

88
00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:25.540
Have you done it?
你体验过吗？

89
00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:26.540
It's so fun.
太好玩了。

90
00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:30.160
We did it with our kids and they'll pull people up on stage
我们带孩子去过，他们会把人叫上台，

91
00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.900
and you'll each get like a different sound effect
每个人会分到一个不同的音效，

92
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.660
and you have to like watch the screen
你得盯着屏幕，

93
00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.680
and make the sound effect to go with it.
配合画面做出相应的音效。

94
00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.700
That's so fun.
那太有趣了。

95
00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.640
Yeah, like you'll put shoes on your hands
对，比如你会把鞋子套在手上，

96
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.900
and make clumpy sounds.
发出沉重的脚步声。

97
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:41.680
For a horse.
模拟马蹄声。

98
00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.140
Yeah, it was so cool.
对，太酷了。

99
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.740
Well, thank you, Emma,
那么，谢谢艾玛，

100
00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.400
for writing in to share your Foley fun fact with us.
写信与我们分享你的拟音趣闻。

101
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.940
Lastly, before we get to our breakdown,
最后，在我们开始解析之前，

102
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:52.120
there is one more deleted scene that we wanted to play
还有一段删减片段我们想放出来，

103
00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.400
because many of you have noted
因为你们很多人都注意到，

104
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.440
that Jim and Angela rarely have scenes together
吉姆和安吉拉在整部剧中，

105
00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.600
where they actually speak to one another
几乎很少有直接对话的场景。

106
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.080
throughout the entire series.
我是说整部剧下来。

107
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.760
I'm not talking about like if we're in a conference room,
我指的不是那种我们在会议室里共处一室的情况，

108
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.300
I'm talking about Jim and Angela having a back and forth.
我说的是吉姆和安吉拉那种一来一回的对话。

109
00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.920
Yes, this was very similar,
没错，这和人们观察到斯坦利和克里德，

110
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.220
the observation that Stanley and Creed
几乎从不说话的情况非常相似。

111
00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:13.000
almost never speak to each other.
确实如此。

112
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:13.300
That's right.
没错。

113
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.300
All right, well, you talked about this scene
好了，你们在最初的解析中提到过这个片段，

114
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.120
in our initial breakdown, but we didn't play it.
但我们当时没放出来。

115
00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.600
And I really thought we needed to hear
我真的觉得我们有必要听听，

116
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:22.560
one of these few times that Jim and Angela speak directly to one another.
吉姆和安吉拉为数不多的直接对话之一。

117
00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.880
Jim has just returned to the Scranton branch
吉姆刚回到斯克兰顿分部，

118
00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.120
and is talking to Kevin over in accounting.
正在会计部和凯文聊天。

119
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.000
Let's hear it.
我们来听听看。

120
00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:28.960
Hey, Kev.
嘿，凯文。

121
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.020
Hey, man.
嘿，伙计。

122
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:30.540
How you doing?
最近怎么样？

123
00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:31.080
Good.
挺好的。

124
00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:36.380
Listen, my M&Ms are under the desk if you want any.
听着，我的M&M豆在桌子底下，你想吃的话随便拿。

125
00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:37.880
Okay.
好的。

126
00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:39.260
Hidden.
藏起来了。

127
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.030
Smart.
聪明。

128
00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:45.870
Good.
不错。

129
00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:48.370
Hey, Angela.
嘿，安吉拉。

130
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.410
You need a haircut.
你该剪头发了。

131
00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:51.570
Bye, Angela.
再见，安吉拉。

132
00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:52.410
All right, Kev.
好了，凯文。

133
00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:53.210
See you later, Jim.
回头见，吉姆。

134
00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:53.570
See you later.
回头见。

135
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.530
It's his first day back.
这是他回来的第一天。

136
00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.890
His hair's flipping out on the sides.
他的头发两边都翘起来了。

137
00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:02.840
I like it.
我挺喜欢的。

138
00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.180
Oh, my Lord.
噢，天哪。

139
00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.540
I mean, I think this might be why he doesn't speak to Angela.
我是说，我觉得这可能就是他不跟安吉拉说话的原因。

140
00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:09.900
I know.
我懂。

141
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.280
I know.
我懂。

142
00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:16.020
Also, that last line, obviously, you know, I talked about this, I improvised it, but could
还有，最后那句台词，显然，你知道，我之前说过，是我即兴发挥的，但

143
00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.880
it be more not in character?
还有比这更不像她人设的吗？

144
00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:18.900
Oh, my Lord.
噢，天哪。

145
00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:19.940
That's true.
确实。

146
00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.300
Well, now, you guys, here is the breakdown of the merger.
好了，各位，现在开始解析合并那一集。

147
00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.220
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

148
00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.540
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

149
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.820
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

150
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.080
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

151
00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.900
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正专为你制作“办公室终极重温”播客。

152
00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:40.260
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享独家幕后故事，

153
00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:42.880
stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
这些故事只有我们两个亲历者才能告诉你。

154
00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.020
We're The Office ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

155
00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:49.390
It's The Merger.
这一集是《合并》。

156
00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:50.850
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

157
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.090
We're merging.
我们要合并了。

158
00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.470
Where are we merging, too?
我们要合并到哪里去？

159
00:05:54.230 --> 00:06:00.590
We are merging two worlds today, Angela, the Stanford and the Scranton branches.
安吉拉，今天我们要合并两个世界，斯坦福分部和斯克兰顿分部。

160
00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:05.550
Not all of the Stanford branch, but some will be merging with Scranton.
不是整个斯坦福分部，但有一部分人会和斯克兰顿合并。

161
00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:09.470
I also feel like we're merging as friends because I'm looking at you.
我也觉得我们作为朋友也在合并，因为我正看着你。

162
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.490
I think we have almost the same outfit on today.
我觉得我们今天穿得几乎一模一样。

163
00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:18.830
You know, I mean, seriously, like they always say like pet owners start to look like their pets.
你知道，我是说真的，就像人们常说的，宠物主人会变得越来越像他们的宠物。

164
00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:23.150
Best friends start to look like each other and like husbands and wives and partners.
最好的朋友会变得越来越像对方，夫妻和伴侣也是如此。

165
00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:25.970
Like, I feel like we're starting to look like each other.
我觉得我们也开始变得越来越像对方了。

166
00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:27.430
We might be.
也许吧。

167
00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:31.490
Also, neither one of us has had a haircut or a hair color in a very long time.
而且，我们俩都很久没剪头发或染头发了。

168
00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.470
I did my own hair color, lady.
我自己染的头发，女士。

169
00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.550
I did too.
我也是。

170
00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:39.150
Well, actually, Lee did mine with my hair colorist on FaceTime.
